---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Home
pageTitle: Jaunita Flessas — Accessibility leader, trainer & maker
permalink: /
navCta:
  label: View services
  url: /services/
extraScripts: ["/assets/js/contact.js"]
---
<div class="wrap">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
    <div class="hero-body">
      {%- if home.available %}
      <p class="hero-availability"><span class="tag tag-accent">Available for contract work</span></p>
      {%- endif %}
      <h1 class="hero-title" id="hero-h"><span>Access is not a feature.</span> <span>It’s the point.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-intro">I’m Jaunita Flessas — an internationally recognised digital accessibility leader, attorney, trainer and maker based in Melbourne. I take on contract work in accessibility, training, instructional design, writing, AI web development and photography — and I bring all of it to the causes I care about: disability rights, human rights, anti-poverty and education.</p>
      <p class="hero-note">Founder of <a href="{{ site.links.empower }}">Empower Accessibility</a> — enterprise accessibility consulting lives there. This site is everything I do as me.</p>
      <ul class="tag-list hero-tags" role="list" aria-label="Credentials">
        {%- for credential in home.credentials %}
        <li class="tag tag-neutral">{{ credential }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a href="{{ "/services/" | url }}" class="btn btn-primary">View services</a>
        <a href="{{ "/speaking/" | url }}" class="btn btn-ghost">See my talks</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-portrait lighten">
      <img src="{{ home.portrait.src | url }}" alt="{{ home.portrait.alt }}"
           width="{{ home.portrait.width }}" height="{{ home.portrait.height }}"
           fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="track-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="track-h" class="visually-hidden">Track record</h2>
    {#- A description list: each number is the term, what it counts is the
        description. Read in order, a pair says "17,000 — employees reached". -#}
    <dl class="stats">
      {%- for stat in home.stats %}
      <div>
        <dt class="stat-value">{{ stat.value }}</dt>
        <dd class="stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</dd>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap">
  <section class="section-values" aria-labelledby="values-h">
    <p class="kicker">What I stand for</p>
    <h2 id="values-h" class="section-title">Values-driven, by design</h2>
    <p class="prose">I look for work that moves the needle on the things that matter. If your project sits in one of these spaces, I want to hear about it — and my rates reflect that.</p>
    <ul class="grid grid-cards" role="list">
      {%- for value in home.values %}
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="card-kicker">{{ value.title }}</h3>
        <p class="card-body">{{ value.body }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="services-h">
    <p class="kicker">What I do</p>
    <h2 id="services-h" class="visually-hidden">Services</h2>
    <ol class="svc-list" role="list">
      {%- for service in home.services %}
      <li class="svc-row">
        <p class="svc-num">{{ service.num }}</p>
        <h3 class="svc-title">{{ service.title }}</h3>
        <p class="svc-copy">{{ service.copy }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p class="btn-row"><a href="{{ "/services/" | url }}" class="btn btn-secondary">All services in detail</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="projects-h">
    <p class="kicker">Featured projects</p>
    <h2 id="projects-h" class="section-title">Things I’ve built and lead</h2>
    <ul class="grid grid-projects" role="list">
      {%- for project in home.projects %}
      <li class="card">
        <p class="card-kicker">{{ project.role }}</p>
        <h3 class="card-title post-title">{{ project.name }}</h3>
        <p class="card-body">{{ project.copy }}</p>
        {%- if project.href %}
        <p class="card-link"><a href="{{ project.href }}">{{ project.linkLabel }}<span class="visually-hidden"> (external site)</span></a></p>
        {%- endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="split split-photo" aria-labelledby="photo-h">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Photography</p>
      <h2 id="photo-h" class="section-title">Behind the lens</h2>
      <p class="prose prose-narrow">Events, portraits and the places my hiking boots take me. Client galleries are delivered through Picflow — proofing, selects and downloads in one accessible place.</p>
      <p class="btn-row"><a href="{{ site.links.picflow }}" class="btn btn-ghost">Browse the full gallery on Picflow<span class="visually-hidden"> (external site)</span></a></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="lighten">
      <img src="{{ home.photograph.src | url }}" alt="{{ home.photograph.alt }}"
           width="{{ home.photograph.width }}" height="{{ home.photograph.height }}"
           loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="quote-section" aria-labelledby="quote-h">
    <h2 id="quote-h" class="visually-hidden">What people say</h2>
    <figure>
      <blockquote class="quote">“{{ home.quote.text }}”</blockquote>
      <figcaption class="quote-attribution">— {{ home.quote.attribution }}</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <hr class="hr">

  <section id="hire" class="section-hire" aria-labelledby="hire-h">
    <p class="kicker">Hire me</p>
    <h2 id="hire-h" class="section-title">Two ways to work with me</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-wide">
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-kicker">Contract &amp; fractional</h3>
        <p class="card-body">Project-based or ongoing: audits, training, courseware, writing, accessible builds and photography — scoped to your timeline. Fractional accessibility leadership if you need a program stood up without a full-time hire.</p>
        <p class="btn-row"><a href="{{ "/services/" | url }}" class="btn btn-secondary">See services</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-kicker">Full-time</h3>
        <p class="card-body">I’m also open to the right permanent role — remote, or hybrid in Melbourne. US citizen with full Australian working rights. Roles I’m qualified for:</p>
        <ul class="tag-list hero-tags" role="list" aria-label="Roles I’m qualified for">
          {%- for role in home.roles %}
          <li class="tag tag-outline">{{ role }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p class="btn-row"><a href="#contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Send me a role</a></p>
        <p class="resume-links">Role-specific résumés (accessible HTML · tagged-PDF ready):
          {%- for cv in resumes.items %}
          <a href="{{ ("/resume/" + cv.slug + "/") | url }}">{{ cv.label }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}
          {%- endfor %}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="section-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-h">
    <h2 id="contact-h" class="section-title-sm">Let’s find the work that matters</h2>
    <p class="prose">Contract, fractional or project-based — if it advances access, rights, education or opportunity, I’m interested. Based in Melbourne, working with the US, EU, Canada and Australia.</p>
    {#- How this sends is set in src/_data/site.js.

        "mailto" (the design's own behaviour) opens the reader's own email app
        with everything pre-filled. That needs JavaScript, so the Send button
        is created by the script rather than sitting dead in the HTML, and the
        <noscript> block below says so before anyone fills the form in.

        No branch ever renders the email address into the markup. -#}
    {%- if site.form.provider != "none" %}
    {%- set isMailto = site.form.provider == "mailto" %}
    <form class="contact-form" id="contact-form" name="contact"
          {%- if isMailto %} method="post" data-send="mailto"
          {%- elif site.form.provider == "formspree" %} method="POST" action="{{ site.form.endpoint }}"
          {%- else %} method="POST" action="{{ site.form.successUrl }}"{% endif %}
          aria-labelledby="contact-h">
      {%- if site.form.provider == "netlify" %}
      <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="contact">
      {%- elif site.form.provider == "formspree" %}
      <input type="hidden" name="_next" value="{{ site.url }}{{ site.form.successUrl }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="[jaunitaflessas.com] New message">
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if isMailto %}
      {#- Said before the fields, not after, so nobody fills in a form that
          cannot send. -#}
      <noscript>
        <p class="form-notice">This form hands your message to your own email app, which needs JavaScript — and it’s switched off in your browser, so the fields below won’t send. <a href="{{ site.links.linkedin }}">Message me on LinkedIn</a> instead, and I’ll pick it up there.</p>
      </noscript>
      {%- endif %}
      <div class="field">
        <label for="cf-name">Your name</label>
        <input id="cf-name" name="name" class="input" type="text" required autocomplete="name">
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="cf-email">Your email</label>
        <input id="cf-email" name="email" class="input" type="email" required autocomplete="email">
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="cf-topic">What’s this about?</label>
        <select id="cf-topic" name="topic" class="input" required>
          {%- for topic in home.contactTopics %}
          <option value="{{ topic }}">{{ topic }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="cf-msg">Message</label>
        <textarea id="cf-msg" name="message" class="input" rows="5" required></textarea>
      </div>
      {#- Spam trap. Off-screen, unfocusable and hidden from assistive tech, so
          only a bot filling every field will trip it. -#}
      <div class="honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
        <label for="cf-company">Leave this field empty</label>
        <input id="cf-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
      {#- The Send button is inserted here by contact.js. LinkedIn is a plain
          link and is always available, script or no script. -#}
      <div class="btn-row contact-actions">
        <a href="{{ site.links.linkedin }}" class="btn btn-ghost">LinkedIn<span class="visually-hidden"> (external site)</span></a>
      </div>
      {#- Empty at load, and present at load: a live region has to already be in
          the page for what gets put into it to be announced. -#}
      <p class="contact-status" id="contact-status" role="status"></p>
      {#- For the mailto form this starts hidden and is revealed by the script,
          because it describes what pressing Send does — and without scripting
          there is no Send. The <noscript> block above covers that case. -#}
      <p class="contact-note" id="contact-note"{% if isMailto %} hidden{% endif %}>
        {%- if isMailto %}Sending opens your own email app with everything pre-filled — nothing is submitted to this site.
        {%- else %}Everything here reaches me directly. I read it all myself.{% endif %}
      </p>
    </form>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  <section class="section-a11y" aria-labelledby="a11y-h">
    <h2 id="a11y-h" class="card-title">Accessibility statement</h2>
    <p class="prose prose-wide">This site is built to WCAG 2.2 AA: semantic structure, full keyboard operability, visible focus, alt text on images and no motion that can’t be paused. If you hit a barrier anywhere, <a href="#contact">tell me through the contact form</a> — I’ll fix it and credit you.</p>
  </section>
</div>
